# Relations this migration declares, parsed and paired with its migration by
# db-schema/tests/schema_fence.rs. No test checks them against a database:
# the container tests named below were deleted with the old stack's
# Postgres tests, so their claims are history, not current coverage.
#
# One nullable ADD COLUMN against a table 0011 created, plus a `COMMENT ON
# COLUMN`. Neither is a relation, so the existence probe is blind to it — the
# same position 0019_fair_price_fx_tape_live is in.
#
# The column is asserted by its writer and reader instead:
# `crypto_leg_outlier_names_the_dispersed_legs_outlier` in
# market-data/tests/fair_price_roundtrip.rs writes it through
# `fair_price_insert.sql` and reads it back.
none alters a table 0011 created — adds one nullable column and its comment, not a relation
